entation is available  on github so um you can maybe get it now  and  take a look at some of the code or you  can just follow the presentation and  maybe after the talk you can get the  code and play around with it run it  break it and see that you are able to  run the tests and i also configure  github actions so that you can see the  continuous integration thing  so hope you can get the code and enjoy  and play around with it so now let's get  started with the actual framework and  i developed this framework over um like  a couple of years i i couldn't find like  a really clear way of explaining  how i was testing my code until like a  few years of experimenting trying out  new things  um  and i think i finally after after a few  years i got this this clear idea of okay  we have to do this in different levels  and as we make progress we generate more  uh more robust tests so i think this is  this i would say this is the sim um like  the summary of my experience  and that's why i want to share that with  you so we are going to have five  different levels and the idea is that as  we make progress on our project we want  to keep increasing and increasing the  the robustness of our tests so let's  start with the first one the first one  is called smoke testing and this is the  most basic type of testing that we can  apply and it's called smoke testing  because we are  not  testing the output we are not doing  anything specific we are just making  sure that our code runs so this is the  most basic thing ima imagine you  just started working on a machine  learning project and you have some code  that maybe gets some data clean some  data you generate your first couple  features you want to make sure that you  are able to get a clean  um  server install your dependencies and run  your code  now  a really important uh question that you  may have is well if i have um 10  gigabytes of data or maybe even more  like one terabyte of data how am i going  to be testing this cont